    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393-a1">

                <pb facs="0759" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg649"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    355.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Sobral to Señor Diéguez</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 23,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister Diéguez</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mexico:</hi></p>
                <p>The so-called government of Salvador has declared war on Guatemala after having
                    begun the same, invading our territory with fire and sword. My Government has
                    been forced to accept the war, and the army is being actively mobilized to
                    sustain with dignity the struggle; the foreign colonies, business interests, and
                    the people en masse have hastened to offer their services for the defense of the
                    country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Martinez Sobral.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
